      "content": "i get what u mean about socio-economics and all that. but if i'm just looking at it from a practical travel perspective, isn't it just a reality that some of the more 'traditional' or white neighborhoods like Richmond or Chelsea are just naturally more peaceful? it feels like there's a definite pattern where the more diverse the area gets, the more chaotic it becomes. is it even possible to find areas that are both really diverse and culture-rich but still have that sense of safety and order you find in the more established, white parts of london?",
